  <h1>The Riemann Dossier</h1>
  <p class="lede muted">Fifty-two files record an ambitious search through kernels, zero sums, quadratic
    forms and spectral operators. This dossier keeps the exact mathematics, the finite evidence and the
    corrections on separate lines. It does not contain or claim a proof of the Riemann Hypothesis.</p>
</section>

<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame frame--first illuminated">
    <p class="kicker">Consolidated 14 October 2026</p>
    <h2 id="t-rh-reading-rule">The last filename is not the last word</h2>
    <p class="lede">The source archive is a research diary. Seven files call themselves comprehensive, but
      each accumulates earlier claims and later addenda rather than replacing a corrected argument cleanly.</p>
    <p>The archive expands to 52 documents and 916,946 bytes. Four pairs are exact duplicates, leaving 48
      unique payloads. Its sessions repeatedly do something scientifically valuable: make a strong claim,
      test it, discover a sign, normalisation or logical error, and record a correction. The same structure
      creates a danger. A theorem announced near the top of a master file may be retracted hundreds of lines
      later and then reappear in a final summary. Consolidation therefore cannot mean choosing the most recent
      or most confident sentence. It means reconstructing each claim through its correction history.</p>
    <p>This section uses four grades. <span class="sci">&#9670; Exact or internally derivable</span> means the
      displayed calculation can be reproduced from its stated assumptions. <span class="hist">&#9670; Source
      report</span> means the archive attributes a result to an external paper that this internal audit has not
      independently certified. <span class="spec">&#9670; Numerical or conditional</span> means finite evidence,
      an RH-dependent formula or an incomplete proof programme. <span class="myth">&#9670; Retracted or
      unsupported</span> marks a claim the supplied argument does not establish.</p>
    <p>The full source reconciliation and line of reasoning are retained in the project document
      <code>docs/rh/RH_CONSOLIDATED_AUDIT.md</code>. The public pages are an accessible account of that audit,
      not a replacement for it.</p>
  </div>
</section>

